  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1032 PM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nA bigger story for us is the anticipated hard freeze this weekend. \nThis will be our first widespread hard freeze, so make sure you are \ntaking care of pets, outdoor or exposed pipes, sensitive plants, and \nchecking on people around you who may be sensitive to the cold. Lows \nthis weekend will be in the mid 20s areawide, with highs in the 50s \ncontinuing into the start of the work week.\n\nAfter our exciting flurries in the east, a surface ridge will build \nin over Middle Tennessee for the work week. Highs will warm into the \n60s by mid-week, with lows staying chilly in the 30s and 40s. This \nsurface high will also help keep us precipitation free, which is not \nanticipated to help the ongoing drought.",
